.TH VISIONFS 4
.SH NAME
visionfs \- recognition as files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B visionfs
[
.B -S
] [
.B -m
.I mountpoint
] [
.B -s
.I spec
] [
.B load
.I name dir
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Visionfs
serves recognition models as files, mounted by default at
.BR /mnt/vision :
a program, a person at the shell, or an agent writes a picture and
reads back what is in it, one record a line.
Which machine does the looking is which server is mounted there: this
one, or another's, over 9P.
.PP
A model is a directory made by
.BR tools/vision/onnx2vis.py :
.BR graph ,
.BR weights ,
.BR classes ,
.B info
and
.BR sha256 .
Its weights are refused unless their SHA-256 is the one recorded, and
its graph is checked, every operation's numbers and every tensor's
shape, before anything runs.
It is run by
.B /dis/lib/visnet.dis
on
.BR $Tensor ,
the processor's arithmetic (see
.IR tensor (2)).
.PP
.B -s
posts the server in
.BR #s
as
.I spec
(default
.BR vision ),
so a VM other than the one it runs in can mount it (see
.IR vm (1));
.B -S
posts nothing.
.I Load
loads a model as the server starts, as
.B ctl
does.
.SS Files
.TF models/\fIname\fP/classes
.TP
.B ctl
Written:
.BI load " name dir"
loads the model in
.I dir
as
.IR name ;
.BI unload " name"
lets it go, refused while a session uses it.
Read: the engine
.RB ( "engine cpu" ),
where a session may run
.RB ( "places cpu" ),
and each model,
.BI model " name dir" .
.TP
.BI models/ name /info
.B kind=detect decode=yolox input=416x416 classes=80 order=bgr fill=114 places=cpu sha256=...
.TP
.BI models/ name /classes
One class name a line, in index order.
.TP
.B clone
Read: a new session's number,
.IR N .
The session lasts while any of its files is open, this one included.
.TP
.IB N /ctl
A setting a line, written as read:
.BI model " name" \fR,
.B place cpu\fR,
.BI thresh " r"
(0 to 1; 0.30 at first),
.BI iou " r"
(boxes of one class overlapping by this or more are kept once; 0.45),
.BI classes " name ..."
or
.BR "classes all" .
Every line of a write is checked before any is done, and a refusal says
why.
A new session has the first model loaded.
.TP
.IB N /image
A picture, in any format
.IR imgload (2)
reads or a binary PPM, in as many writes as it takes from its start; it
is looked at when the file is closed.
.TP
.IB N /detections
What was found in the last picture, best first, one record a line:
.IP
.EX
class=dog score=0.86 x0=133 y0=207 x1=326 y1=543
.EE
.IP
in the picture's pixels,
.B x0 y0
inside the box and
.B x1 y1
just past it.
A read waits while the picture is looked at.
Nothing found is nothing read.
.TP
.IB N /layer/vision. N
The same records, as a layer to bind into a video's stack.
.TP
.IB N /status
.BI state= state
.RB ( idle ,
.BR running ,
.BR ready ,
.BR error )
and
.BI model= name\fR,
with
.BI reason= ...
when something is wrong.
.TP
.IB N /stats
.BI images= n
looked at,
.BI found= n
in the last,
.BI ms= n
it took.
.PD
.PP
Each picture is looked at in a process of its own, so one session's
never holds up another's, nor the server.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
; visionfs load nano /lib/vision/yolox-nano
; {
	id=`{read}
	cat photo.jpg > /mnt/vision/$id/image
	cat /mnt/vision/$id/detections
} < /mnt/vision/clone
class=dog score=0.86 x0=133 y0=207 x1=326 y1=543
class=bicycle score=0.80 x0=54 y0=137 x1=572 y1=423
.EE
.PP
On a machine with no model of its own, another's:
.EX
; mount tcp!orin!vision /mnt/vision
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/visionfs.b
.br
.B /appl/lib/visnet.b
.br
.B /tools/vision/onnx2vis.py
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR vision (1),
.IR tensor (2)
.SH BUGS
Pictures only: following a video feed
.RB ( src )
is refused, saying so, until it is served.
Only detectors of the YOLOX family are converted, and only the
processor's engine is served here.
